.TH draw 1 "November 2026" "Motif"
.SH NAME
draw \- Motif Paint raster drawing demonstration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B draw
.RI [ "Xt options" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Draw is a Paint-style drawing application. A compact toolbar and color palette
sit above a canvas that fits the window. Zoom enables scrollbars only when the
picture exceeds the viewport. Window resizing never resamples the document.
.SH TOOLS
Tool and action buttons use centered, scalable classic icons with hover tooltips.
The palette uses two rows of square color swatches.
Pencil, Brush, Eraser, Line, Rectangle, Ellipse, Fill, Eyedropper, Text and
rectangular Select are available in the left tool panel. Size controls the
brush, eraser and shape thickness. Solid shapes fills rectangles and ellipses.
Right-button drawing uses white. Ink accepts a custom hexadecimal RGB color.
Text places an X11 bitmap label. Select a rectangle before Copy or Cut; Paste
places the session-local clipboard at the next canvas click.
.SH FILES
Open and Save support uncompressed 24-bit BMP. Builds configured with libpng
also support PNG; transparency is flattened onto white. The filename extension
chooses the save format. A failed load does not replace the current picture.
Unsaved changes and replacement of existing files are confirmed.
.SH EDITING
Undo and Redo retain sixteen edits. Canvas size crops or extends the picture
without resampling and can be undone. The initial document is 960 by 640 pixels;
width and height are bounded to 1 through 4096 pixels. TrueColor X11 is required.
.SH KEYS
Ctrl+N/O/S: New/Open/Save. Ctrl+Shift+S: Save As. Ctrl+Z/Y: Undo/Redo.
Ctrl+C/X/V: Copy/Cut/Paste. Delete: clear selection, or canvas if none.
Escape: cancel drawing or paste. Plus/minus: zoom. Zero: fit.
.SH HELP
The Help menu contains the drawing guide.
